# Dot UI rule (Presentation layer for .NET UI apps)

(Canonical: development-guides/DOT_ARCHITECTURE.md. Base rule: .cursor/rules/dot.mdc and DOT_ARCHITECTURE.md.)

**Conflict precedence:** If any other document or rule conflicts with this rule on UI structure, Presentation layer, or Fluent 2 conventions, follow DOT_ARCHITECTURE.md and this rule.

When building **UI** in dotapps (WPF, MAUI, Blazor Hybrid, or Avalonia):

1. **Layers.** Follow Clean Architecture: Domain (no deps) → Application (use cases, DTOs, CQRS/MediatR) → Infrastructure (EF, APIs, auth) → Presentation (Views, ViewModels, no business logic).

2. **Presentation structure.** Use Assets/ (Fonts, Images, Styles), Components/, Pages or Views/ (by feature), ViewModels/ (with Base/), Services/ (Navigation, Dialog), Converters/.

3. **Naming.** Views: [Feature]Page/Window/View; ViewModels: [Feature]ViewModel; Services: I[Name]Service; Commands: [Action]Command; async: [Method]Async.

4. **Design.** Fluent 2: Mica/Acrylic, shadows/strokes, motion (staggered list, drill-in navigation), Segoe UI Variable, Light/Dark support.

5. **Language.** English and ASCII in code (per dot.mdc). Root namespace DotApps.<AppName>.

Do not duplicate base dot rules (layout, dependencies, DotCore.*) here; see DOT_ARCHITECTURE.md and dot.mdc.
